    "question": {
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}24u - 6v &=0 \\\\ 4u + 5v &=-24\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $u$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $u$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that the coefficient of $u$ in the first equation is $24$, while in the second equation it is $4$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-6$, then the coefficient of $u$ will turn into $-24$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $24$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}24u - 6v &=0 \\\\ 4u + 5v &=-24 && \\times (-6)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThis gives the equivalent system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}24u - 6v &=0 \\\\ -24u - 30v &=144\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $u$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cancel{24u} - 6v &= 0 \\\\\n\\cancel{-24u} - 30v &= 144 \\\\\n(-6v - 30v) &= (0 + 144) \\\\\n-36v &= 144 \\\\\nv &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*Multiply the $\\text{second}$ equation by $-6$, and add the equations*.",
